  { .code = "TemperatureBasedLength";        .bovnar = "m/K";                 .reverse = false; },
  # A DIFFERENCE, and now there is a unit that says so. This row read "K" until
  # the Δ units existed, which made qudt-qk:TemperatureDifference and
  # qudt-qk:ThermodynamicTemperature the same unit -- the exact confusion the
  # code's own name rules out, and one that converts to °F wrong by 255.37.
  # A quantity KIND states a quantity and no unit, so there is no published unit
  # string to diverge from here: ΔK is the faithful reading of the name.
  #
  # The CF standard names that are also differences (air_temperature_anomaly and
  # its three siblings) are deliberately NOT changed the same way: CF states
  # canonical_units = "K" for them, and overriding a publisher's stated unit from
  # its name is a different decision -- see doc/temperature_difference.md §7.
  # It reverses, unlike the rest of this tail: ΔK is claimed by no other quantity
  # kind, so there is exactly one code to write it back as, and gen_profiles.py's
  # coverage check is right to insist the question be answered rather than left
  # to the block's default.
